[0.003, "o", "\u001b[1;39m{\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"model\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"llama3.2\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"usage\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m{\r\n    \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"prompt_tokens\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m37\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n    \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"completion_tokens\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m423\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n    \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"total_tokens\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m460\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\r\n  \u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"choices\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m[\r\n    \u001b[1;39m{\r\n      \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"message\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m{\r\n        \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"content\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"I'm a large language model, I don't have real-time access to the latest technology or models. However, I can give you an overview of the architecture and components of language models like myself, which are based on transformer-based architectures.\\n\\nSome of the current state-of-the-art language models include:\\n\\n1. **BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representation from Transformers)**: Developed by Google in 2018, BERT is designed for natural language processing tasks such as question-answ"]
[0.000, "o", "ering, sentiment analysis, and text classification.\\n2. **RoBERTa (Robustly Optimized BERT Pretraining Approach)**: Introduced in 2019, RoBERTa is a variant of BERT that uses a different approach to optimize its performance on various NLP tasks.\\n3. **XLNet**: Released in 2019, XLNet is designed for question-answering and other complex NLP tasks. It features a new architecture that incorporates self-supervised learning and fine-tuning.\\n4. **Longformer**: Introduced in 2020, Longformer is a transformer-based model that uses a different approach to handle long-range dependencies and context.\\n5. **T5 (Transformers for Task-Performing Models)**: Announced in 2019, T5 is designed to scale to smaller input tokens while maintaining high performance on sequence-to-sequence tasks.\\n\\nThese models often involve complex architectures like:\\n\\n1. **Multi-layer Perceptrons (MLPs) or Feedforward Networks**: These deep neural networks are used as classifiers or feature extractors.\\n2. **Self-Attention Mechanism**: This is"]
[0.000, "o", " a key component of the transformer architecture that allows the model to attend to different parts of the input sequence and weigh their importance.\\n3. **Subword Encoders or WordPiece Tokenization**: These are used for word-level tokenization, which helps to reduce dimensionality and improve efficiency.\\n\\nKeep in mind that these architectures and techniques are not exhaustive, and researchers continually explore new variations and innovations to improve NLP performance.\\n\\nWhich specific aspect of language models would you like me to elaborate on?\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n        \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"role\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"assistant\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\r\n      \u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n      \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"index\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39m0\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n      \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"finish_reason\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"stop\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    \u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\r\n  \u001b[1;39m]\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"id\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"chatcmpl-425\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n"]
